meta-kdebug
==========

Optional Yocto layer for enabling kernel debugging support.

Enabling the layer
------------------

Add the layer to `build/conf/bblayers.conf`:

```
/workdir/meta-kdebug
```

Then add the `kdebug` distribution feature to `build/conf/local.conf`:

```
DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " kdebug"
```

Effect
------

When `kdebug` is present in the distribution features, the layer applies a
configuration fragment to the recipe that provides `virtual/kernel`:

```
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT=y
CONFIG_GDB_SCRIPTS=y
```

If `CONFIG_GDB_SCRIPTS=y` is enabled in the final kernel configuration, the
build also generates the kernel GDB scripts in the kernel build directory:

```
vmlinux-gdb.py
scripts/gdb/linux/*.py
```

The layer uses a globally inherited class and therefore does not depend on the
name of the kernel recipe.

Without the `kdebug` feature, the layer does not modify the kernel `SRC_URI`.
